<article class="env-lemma" id="0B7T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B7T">Lemma <span data-tag="0B7T">39.7.12</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $T = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ where $A$ is a directed colimit of algebras which are finite products of copies of $k$. For any scheme $X$ over $k$ we have $|T \times _ k X| = |T| \times |X|$ as topological spaces. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By taking an affine open covering we reduce to the case of an affine $X$. Say $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$. Write $A = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits A_ i$ with $A_ i = \prod _{t \in T_ i} k$ and $T_ i$ finite. Then $T_ i = |\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A_ i)|$ with the discrete topology and the transition morphisms $A_ i \to A_{i'}$ are given by set maps $T_{i'} \to T_ i$. Thus $|T| = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits T_ i$ as a topological space, see Limits, Lemma <a href="/tag/01YY" data-tag="01YY">32.4.6</a>. Similarly we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \begin{align*}  |T \times _ k X| &  = |\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A \otimes _ k B)| \\ &  = |\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits A_ i \otimes _ k B)| \\ &  = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits |\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A_ i \otimes _ k B)| \\ &  = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits |\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\prod \nolimits _{t \in T_ i} B)| \\ &  = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits T_ i \times |X| \\ &  = (\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits T_ i) \times |X| \\ &  = |T| \times |X| \end{align*}
</div>
    <p>
       by the lemma above and the fact that limits commute with limits. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>